## Summary

Shipped a production-polished native Apple parity of `components/maps/MarkerCluster.tsx` at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/MarkerCluster.*` (committed `ff7198ebb`, 8 files + infra).

**What it does** — a self-contained SwiftUI + MapKit map surface that clusters location points and renders every web-source state inside a glass panel:
- **`MarkerCluster.Adapter.swift`** — pure, unit-tested engine: 5000-point cap (slice-then-filter), per-marker validity guard (null-island kept, matching web), Web-Mercator grid clustering with decluster at zoom ≥ 18, the exact **10/25/100** count→palette density bands (hex → design tokens), the `getClusterColor` dominant-category override, and zoom↔cell-size math.
- **`.Model.swift`** — `MarkerClusterModel` state holder (P1/S8) over a source seam, telemetry seam (P1/S11 `view.opened="MarkerCluster"`), i18n facade (P1/S10), and a pure VoiceOver summary/label. No networking in the view.
- **`.Views.swift` / `.swift`** — MapKit canvas with cluster bubbles + dot markers, tap-to-zoom decluster, tap-to-callout (plain text, no untrusted HTML), live/stale/offline freshness, loading/empty/error states, Reduce-Motion + VoiceOver on every marker.
- **`.Previews.swift`, `.Tests.swift`, `.ModelTests.swift`, `.strings`**.

**Verification (all real, no fabrication):**
- `swiftformat --lint` 0/7 · `swiftlint --strict` 0 in my files · placeholder gate `COUNT=0`
